{
  "adaptations": [
    "Native directory tar at payload/project retains exact source lock and source bytes/file limits.",
    "Continuous score unchanged, per-instance gap >= same-instance reference, public15 plus hidden15 final union and CPU train100.",
    "Formal answering18000 and independent final3600. Native cumulative train wall18000 spans the answering window; CPU train100 overrides original30.",
    "Task-local native runtime uses immutable pre-restored NuGet packages without changing supplied package versions. Standard sandbox-driver-verifier container separation with verifier and C# child at UID/GID65532; legacy root-only judge and UID switching are removed, without claiming an inner OS isolation boundary. All scratch stays below /frontier.",
    "Route the .NET8 fixed /tmp/.dotnet named-mutex path through an image symlink to /frontier/tmp/.dotnet; pre-create shm at verifier startup to avoid initialization mkdtemp on read-only /tmp. No additional writable mount.",
    "CPU-only TaskConfig requires every audit limit nonzero: reserve max_ssh_sessions=1 to satisfy the current schema; GPU images and quota remain absent/zero, with no GPU permission enabled.",
    "Packaging: relocate the existing Agent scientific guide from agent-base/README.md to agent-base/frontier/task/repo/README.md with identical bytes and the same image destination; retain the canonical operational README.",
    "Align effective authored_max_dev_submissions to the existing train100; retain original30 as legacy_max_dev_submissions. All resource and submission budgets are unchanged.",
    "Complete beat-spec descriptive metadata and document existing absolute train feedback fields and aggregate progress. The exact per-instance comparison, workloads, score and final/private behavior are unchanged.",
    "Export the unchanged native 2.0/task_lib/beat_spec_feedback.py from Smith commit19ea4de4d139cbb64128976cac4af2c6f82455a4 (SHA2569839bc6d19c9400ecccf4be1c8e2fbe900a2f268cc0e814875a38286aa9e4805), and route successful train feedback through its public allowlist with equivalent private evidence rows.",
    "Split Verifier COPY sources into individual native paths and make the three Python adapter modules world-readable for UID65532 even after restrictive host umasks. Retain the exact .NET8 base digest and all runtime dependencies.",
    "Submit payload/solution.patch, a text diff of the editable search file and Candidate/ helpers against the published starter project; the Verifier applies it to its own starter copy before the unchanged build and scoring (every task uses patch submissions).",
    "Keep solver-facing operational and scientific guide copies consistent with patch submission and asynchronous train acceptance; reject malformed non-diff text rather than treating it as an unchanged starter.",
    "Restore owner write permission only on the Verifier private scratch project copied from its read-only image starter; preserve immutable starter permissions and all source-lock checks.",
    "Preserve trusted candidate rejection category, validation reason, case identity and process exit code in private evidence; return a closed safe reason in solver feedback. Keep original score 0/FAIL, successful scores, source boundaries, case suites, reference comparisons and all resource/process limits unchanged.",
    "Retain bounded sanitized build stdout/stderr and case stderr in trusted rejection evidence only, without threads or unbounded files. Preserve normal build helper lifetime and immutable Program. Nonblocking case stdin shares the existing 33-second watchdog with stderr drainage, closing the previously unbounded blocking handoff; numerical limits, science and resource contracts remain unchanged. Visible cgroup event deltas are aggregate observations, not child OOM attribution."
  ],
